37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial showed a significant 20% drop in readmissions for elderly patients, which reversed once it ended. However, the shared nursing round was highly inefficient, with a third of visits failing. We must prioritize proven efficacy over ambition.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The physical capacity is strained. Outpatient rooms and parking are full by mid-morning, and the shuttle coverage is minimal. Furthermore, the booking system fails to record any activity without a fixed appointment, masking the true workload.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our optimism often outpaces our administration. I've found that joint ventures can collapse when ownership is ambiguous, and our external data agreements move with the speed of a glacier. We must be wary of ""collaborative"" dreams.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh dear, the staffing news is a bit worrying! We have quite a few nursing vacancies and agency costs are going up. But on the bright side, the midwifery rota actually has some extra room!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a sobering reminder that our resources are more fragile than they appear. Our allocation has shrunk, and we must be mindful that off-site care brings no funding, while on-site sessions sustain us.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if on-site sessions are the only way to sustain funding, we should avoid the pitfalls of the shared nursing round. We need a program that is both financially viable and demonstrably effective for patients.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, efficacy is irrelevant if the patient cannot find a parking space or a room. We are already at a breaking point; any program that increases foot traffic or relies on unrecorded labor will likely fail.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, a poignant point. If we invite more guests to a house with no room, we simply create a more crowded disaster. We must seek a program that requires neither new space nor glacial bureaucracy.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, @Benjamin, you're right that we're crowded! But we can't forget the people working there. If we pick something that adds more pressure to the already empty nursing posts, it'll just make everyone sad and tired!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Servas,,"My dear friends, your concerns are the threads that weave a complete picture. We must seek a path that honors our staff's well-being while remaining grounded in the reality of our dwindling coffers. Balance is the key to longevity.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, I agree that staff pressure is a risk, but we cannot ignore that the call-back trial actually worked. We should look for a program that mimics that success without adding to the physical congestion @Toshio mentioned.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, a program that mimics the call-back trial might work, provided it is remote or digital. If it requires physical presence or adds unrecorded administrative tasks, it will only exacerbate our current systemic congestion.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, a digital solution sounds delightful in theory, provided it doesn't require those aforementioned glacial data agreements. I suspect any ""seamless"" integration with outside partners is a fantasy we cannot afford to indulge.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that sounds so scary! I just want us to pick something that doesn't make the nurses cry. Since midwifery has some slack, maybe we can find a way to help them out or use that space?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see us seeking a middle path. Let us remember that a program is not merely a goal, but a living commitment. We must ensure it is truly affordable for the long term.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have a clear conflict between proven patient outcomes and severe resource constraints. We must avoid any proposal that relies on external partnerships or physical space. A low-impact, high-efficacy internal program is our only logical choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Any proposal that increases physical traffic or relies on the current booking system's flaws is a liability. We must prioritize a program that is lean, internal, and requires minimal physical infrastructure to avoid a total system seizure.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a rare moment of consensus. We require a program that is internally managed, physically unobtrusive, and devoid of bureaucratic entanglement. Let us hope the candidates are less ambitious than our imagination.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I hope the candidates are kind to our staff! I'll support whatever we choose, as long as it doesn't put too much pressure on the nurses who are already working so hard. I'm ready for the next part!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Servas,,"The wisdom of consensus is a beautiful thing. We have looked into the mirror of our reality and seen it clearly. Now, let us welcome the candidates with open minds and steady hearts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
