62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Based on our findings, Option A is too similar to the failed shared nursing round, and C is impossible given the parking and room shortages. Option D relies on the external data agreements Benjamin warned us about. Option B is the most logical.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, I agree. Option C is a non-starter due to space and parking. Option A and D risk systemic seizure through unrecorded labor or bureaucratic delays. Option B utilizes the midwifery slack Yumi mentioned and fits our constraints.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, @Toshio, your logic is impeccable. Option B avoids the glacial pace of external agreements and the physical congestion of a new unit. Provided the joint management is clearly defined, it is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option B sounds perfect! It uses the extra room in the midwifery rota, so it won't stress out the other nurses, and it's such a lovely way to help new parents! I'm all for it!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a gentle joy to see such harmony. Option B aligns with our needs, as it remains on-site to secure our funding while utilizing existing capacity. It is a sustainable seed for a bright future.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Since we are all in agreement, there is no need for further debate. Option B is the only candidate that satisfies our requirements for efficacy, financial sustainability, and operational feasibility without overloading our strained resources.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I concur. Option B is the only proposal that does not threaten to seize up our already saturated physical and digital infrastructure. It is the most prudent choice for the hospital's stability.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure when the path of least resistance is also the path of most reason. Option B is the only candidate that doesn't invite a bureaucratic or physical catastrophe. I am fully in support.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so happy we all agree! Option B is a wonderful choice that helps families and keeps our staff smiling. I'm voting for Option B with all my heart!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Servas,,"When the heart and the mind speak the same language, the path forward is clear. Option B is a prudent choice that respects our limits while nurturing our community. I shall cast my vote for it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
